{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"dizzy-abysmal-fox","creation_channel":"python","description":"## Context\nREADME workflow prose conflicts with current claim, graph, help, and close behavior. The dispatcher fix on `chartreuse-interested-viper`, the assignee correction on `weariless-scrapable-mouse`, the quickstart work on `tsunamic-wax-hog`, and ADR 0100 define the historical basis. F12 completed command discovery before this story finalized help wording.\n\n## Plan\n- Document default claim assignment and Jira-resolvable explicit overrides.\n- Name all seven relations, including `caused_by`.\n- Document optional relation-scoped unlink.\n- Describe help recognition before `--` while preserving nested `bridge` and `audit` handling.\n- Describe integrated completion verification for task, bug, story, and epic closes as an optional gate that is disabled by default and enabled with `verify.require_completion_verification_for_close`.\n- Preserve the tested quickstart and existing README structure.\n- Compare README wording against the behavior exercised by `tests/unit/test_claim_default_assignee.py`, `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_event_schema_relations.py`, `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_unlink_relation_scoped_e39f.py`, `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_create_help_no_write_b8de.py`, and `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_completion_gate.py`.\n- Leave demonstration assets for F16.\n\n## Verification\n- D1 runs `python scripts/check_docs_index.py --check`.\n- D2 runs `python scripts/check_readme_quickstart.py`.\n- D3 runs `python -m pytest tests/scripts/test_check_readme_quickstart.py -q`.\n- D4 runs `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_claim_default_assignee.py tests/interfaces/contracts/test_event_schema_relations.py tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_unlink_relation_scoped_e39f.py tests/interfaces/contracts/test_create_help_no_write_b8de.py tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_completion_gate.py -q`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Generic claim guidance omits an explicit assignee and explains valid overrides.\n- [x] Link guidance names all seven relations.\n- [x] Unlink guidance documents omitted and explicit relation behavior.\n- [x] Help guidance matches leaf and nested command behavior.\n- [x] Close guidance states that ordinary work-ticket completion verification is optional, disabled by default, and enabled with `verify.require_completion_verification_for_close`.\n- [x] The recorded D1 through D4 verification commands pass.\n- [x] No demonstration asset or unrelated README section changes.","id":"063d-5af6-fad9-49bf","parent_id":"fae0-c5dc-cd67-4cf3","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"F08A correct README workflow contracts"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788233399782781001,"uuid":"62c08a87-8803-42b2-99fa-dd2af88acb94"}